  (text "SAO++ power select: the switch common feeds the LEDs. Position 1 = badge 3.3 V, position 2 = OFF (pin 2 unconnected), position 3 = coin cell." (exclude_from_sim no) (at 38.1 38.1 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid "508bddb0-0245-5608-9fa2-8d03777c9199"))
  (text "The badge supply and the coin cell sit on separate switch contacts and are never connected to each other." (exclude_from_sim no) (at 38.1 41.91 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid "cd4dbc27-e406-5735-b184-00dc9cc802b9"))
  (text "LED-only board: SDA, SCL, GPIO1 and GPIO2 are not connected, so no series diode is needed on the cell (see docs/standard.md section 3)." (exclude_from_sim no) (at 38.1 45.72 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid "addd3e88-b14b-52fe-bde2-735a04c1e866"))
  (text "D1 = the robot's left eye as you look at the front, D2 = its right eye. Red through-board LEDs, about 1 mA each through 1.3 k." (exclude_from_sim no) (at 38.1 124.46 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid "c707bb71-f2ba-5904-9b12-e9d2b28c8513"))
  (text "The maker's LED SELECT jumper (LEDs fed from SAO pin 1 or from GPIO2, so a badge could blink them) is not carried over: see the README." (exclude_from_sim no) (at 38.1 128.27 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid "761c7c69-a97b-57d8-97aa-27ebaff01561"))
